  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119784,
      "id": "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54",
      "title": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $C$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "ef845e0c-97c3-5af3-8f18-827098b489bf",
