    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $C$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $1\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "c3bb3d45-9467-5d22-b622-1a5c762831e7",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
