    },
    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $D$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $-8\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $D$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${D}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\n{D}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -8 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "cbe820c9-38cc-5e85-a4fe-7415ce5c2a02",
